[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):
every report that said "wrong date" went into one ticket, and the ticket was marked known with one
fix queued. Read by cause instead of by subject, it holds two problems. Each one got a ticket of its
own, with the number of reports it covers, and each is now closed.

<IssueSplit ticket={4471} {problems} />

<Callout>
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser fix covers the <code>parser</code> reports only. The
<code>hint</code> reports stop because booking-v3 is retired, not because of that fix.
</Callout>

## How the reports were placed

- **By tenant, not by browser.** Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. The cause depends
  on the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`). The tags and the cause disagree on many
  reports, so the counts here never use the tags.
- **Once per id.** The export pages overlap; a report that came twice counts once.
- **Read-as notes stay where they are filed.** The reports the desk read as a one-day move
  (`desk-notes.json`) count under their cause, as the cause table does. A ticket opened for them on
  its own was closed as a duplicate of #1.

## The cause table, as the desk runs it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Merging by subject is fine for the first hour of an incident. Before a merged ticket is marked
  known, split it by cause: a second cause has no fix queued until it has a ticket.
- If date reports keep coming in after the parser fix, they are a new ticket, not #4471.

